# Docker build context is the REPO ROOT (see deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml: context: ..).
#
# deploy/Dockerfile.api only needs two things out of that context:
#   COPY server/          -> the Rust crate (rebuilt inside the image)
#   COPY data/extracted   -> seed content, CAKNA_DATA_DIR
#
# Everything else below is excluded so `docker compose build` on the server
# does not tar ~7 GB of caches and app sources into the daemon.
#
# NOTE: web/build is NOT needed here — docker-compose.prod.yml bind-mounts it
# at runtime (../web/build:/app/static:ro). Excluding it from the build context
# does not affect that mount.

# ── Rust build cache: 4.6 GB, and the image rebuilds it anyway ───────────────
server/target

# ── Flutter app: 2.4 GB, not part of the API image ──────────────────────────
app

# ── Web: node_modules 148 MB; build/ is bind-mounted, not copied ────────────
web

# ── Vendored third-party APKs (398 MB) and the legacy single-file PWA ───────
Tilawah
sample

# ── The superseded Node/Express stack. Kept in the repo because it is still
#    what serves production, but it has no place in the Rust image. ──────────
legacy

# ── Not used by the API image ───────────────────────────────────────────────
brand
tools
docs
data/frontend
*.md

# ── Secrets: deploy/.env is server-only and must never enter an image layer ─
**/.env
deploy/.env

# ── VCS / OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules
*.log
